### Access environment variables in React Native code

Source: https://github.com/expo/expo/blob/main/docs/pages/eas/environment-variables/manage.mdx

Access EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefixed environment variables in client-side code using process.env. This example demonstrates using EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL to dynamically configure the API endpoint for fetch requests in a React Native component.

```typescript
import { Button } from 'react-native';

function Post() {
  const apiUrl = process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL;

  async function onPress() {
    await fetch(apiUrl, {
      /* @hide ... */
      /* @end */
    });
  }

  return <Button onPress={onPress} title="Post" />;
}
```

