### Access environment variables in React Native code

Source: https://github.com/expo/expo/blob/main/docs/pages/guides/environment-variables.mdx

Access EXPO_PUBLIC_ environment variables directly in JavaScript/TypeScript source code using process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_[VARNAME] with dot notation. When running npx expo start, these references are replaced with actual values in the app bundle. Variables update without restarting CLI but require a full reload to see changes in the app.

```tsx
import { Button } from 'react-native';

function Post() {
  const apiUrl = process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL;

  async function onPress() {
    await fetch(apiUrl, { ... })
