### Configure TypeScript path aliases for src directory

Source: https://github.com/expo/expo/blob/main/docs/pages/router/reference/src-directory.mdx

Update tsconfig.json to point TypeScript path aliases to the src directory instead of the root directory. This ensures @/ imports continue working after moving the app directory into src. The default @/* alias should be set to ./src/*.

```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
  }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Configure Path Aliases in tsconfig.json for src Directory

Source: https://github.com/expo/expo/blob/main/docs/pages/router/installation.mdx

Adds path aliases to `tsconfig.json` to simplify import paths, especially when using a `src` directory. This example maps `@/*` to `./src/*`, allowing for cleaner imports like `@/components/button`.

```json
{
  "extends": "expo/tsconfig.base",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true,
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", ".expo/types/**/*.ts", "expo-env.d.ts"]
}
```

--------------------------------

### Configure TypeScript for Expo Router with path aliases

Source: https://github.com/expo/expo/blob/main/docs/pages/router/migrate/from-react-navigation.mdx

Set up tsconfig.json to extend Expo's base configuration and define path aliases for cleaner imports. This configuration enables strict type checking and maps @/* to src/* directories for convenient module resolution.

```json
{
  "extends": "expo/tsconfig.base",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true,
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"],
      "@/assets/*": ["./assets/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", ".expo/types/**/*.ts", "expo-env.d.ts"]
}
```

### Path Aliases > Considerations

Source: https://github.com/expo/expo/blob/main/docs/pages/guides/typescript.mdx

Path aliases allow you to create custom import paths in your project. When using path aliases, you should restart Expo CLI after modifying **tsconfig.json** to update the aliases, though you don't need to clear the Metro cache when the aliases change. If you're not using TypeScript, **jsconfig.json** can serve as an alternative to **tsconfig.json**. Keep in mind that path aliases add additional resolution time when defined, and they are only supported by Metro (including Metro web) and not by the deprecated `@expo/webpack-config`. Bare projects require additional setup for this feature.

### Configure Development Build with Internal Distribution and Simulator

Source: https://github.com/expo/expo/blob/main/docs/pages/custom-builds/schema.mdx

EAS configuration file defining a development build profile that creates an internal distribution build for Android and a simulator build for iOS. The configuration references separate YAML files for platform-specific build steps and credentials injection.

```json
{
  "build": {
    "developmentBuild": {
      "distribution": "internal",
      "android": {
        "config": "development-build-android.yml"
      },
      "ios": {
        "simulator": true,
        "config": "development-build-ios.yml"
      }
    }
  }
}
